WEBVTT

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:37.760
<i>No, no. I need to wake up now.</i>

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:38.970
<i>After all, today is...</i>

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:41.940
New Year's Eve!

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:46.180
Hello, Mom?

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:48.500
Yeah, I'm cleaning up my room.

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:49.180
Nice!

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:50.980
I'll be getting together with other girls.

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:52.810
Oh, Yuno?

00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:55.800
Why aren't you coming home for winter break?

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:59.340
Jeez, honey. I can't hear Yuno's voice.

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:04.280
Yuno, don't mind your dad.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:05.620
We're doing just fine.

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:07.040
Okay!

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:27.190
youki ni kuchibue fuite

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:27.190
Whistling a cheerful tune

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:29.520
madobe no kotori to sesshon

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:29.520
I join the birds chirping by the window

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:32.440
suima ga yatte kite

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:32.440
When fatigue strikes

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:35.070
atama ga danshingu

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:35.070
My imagination runs wild

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:37.530
nan demo kan demo waraeru nichijou

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:37.530
Everything in life makes me smile

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:40.370
okimari na kishoutenketsu

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:40.370
Nothing really new takes place

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:43.000
demo demo tama ni wa piritto supaisu

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:43.000
But sometimes it's exciting to spice things up

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.620
aozora peintingu

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.620
Let's paint it on the blue sky

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:46.670
doko ikou

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:46.670
Where should we go?

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:48.250
koko ni iyou

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:48.250
Let's stay here

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:49.250
sore wa nani

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:49.250
What's that?

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:50.840
are yaritai

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:50.840
I wanna try that!

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:53.420
ima ni tokubetsu na shirushi

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:53.420
Let's make this moment count

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:58.800
tokeibari no mawashikata watashi shidai kamo

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:58.800
How fast my clock moves is all up to me

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:02.470
shiki oriori iro toridori

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:02.470
With a rich palette of colors from the four seasons

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:04.930
nonbiri na everyday

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:04.930
Our laid-back everyday lives can be

00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:07.560
pasuteru bibiddo metoro

00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:07.560
Any blend of pastel, vivid, and metro colors

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:10.400
jibun dake no karaaringu

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:10.400
Anyone can create their own coloring

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.980
sono tokidoki mune doki doki

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.980
So when your heart races in excitement

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:16.700
hachamecha na taiyou ni oegaki

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:16.700
Just draw a sun at the top

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:20.830
tobidasu aatishizumu

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:20.830
And let your inner artist take you from there

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:24.160
gyutto shite ii kana

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:24.160
Can I hold your hand tight?

00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:31.540
suki suki suki wo sukecchi

00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:31.540
I've been sketching everything I love

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:34.080
nijiiro ni somete iku yo

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:34.080
And painting them in rainbow colors

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:38.840
sore ja ittekimasu

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:38.840
All right, I'm off to have some more fun!

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:44.060
December 31st-January 1st,
A Year Going Out,
A Year Coming In

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:46.320
Wishing...

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:47.320
you...

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:48.320
a happy...

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:49.320
new...

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:50.360
year.

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:51.070
All right!

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:54.320
Nazuna, at that pace you won't finish any time this year.

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:59.330
Are New Year's cards delivered the next day if you post them on New Year's Eve?

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:02.920
Th-That won't happen, but they should get it before the new semester begins!

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:05.670
What's wrong, Nazuna-chan?

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:07.920
I tried to talk and write at the same time...

00:03:09.070 --> 00:03:11.920
I'm not sure she'll even finish before the new semester.

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:17.260
At first I was going to make my own stamps.

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:19.020
Huh, you didn't use that?

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:20.520
I wanna make some!

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:23.520
I tried, but I gave up pretty quickly.

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:25.520
This is...

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:28.270
You didn't notice until you were done carving?

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:29.780
I'm done!

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:31.030
Miya-chan, that was fast!

00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:32.280
Wow!

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:33.660
But it says "celebrations."

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:36.030
It doesn't really have the "New Year's" vibe.

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:37.530
But when you use it...

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:38.780
Bam!

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:48.340
Your kotatsu is nice and big, Nazuna-san.

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:50.660
Sorry for inviting ourselves here.

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:51.600
Oh, I don't mind.

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:53.920
My family used to use this table.

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:56.420
Okay, time for a tangerine quiz!

00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:56.940
Huh?

00:03:56.940 --> 00:04:00.660
There are three tangerines in this bag right now.

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:03.310
So when Yamauchi-san the farmer has free time, he likes to...

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:05.430
How are we supposed to know?!

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:06.440
Incorrect.

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:07.940
Nice try, Yunocchi.

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:10.440
Yamauchi-san's hobby is skydiving.

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:11.110
But!

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:13.340
There's more?

00:04:13.340 --> 00:04:15.530
Wait, his hobby is skydiving?!

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:20.080
Which one of these three tangerines is the sweetest?

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:21.980
We can't tell that either!

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:23.790
Then let's taste them and find out.

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:28.790
You can't tell if you eat them all at once!

00:04:33.050 --> 00:04:36.880
The seniors' study sessions end late in the evening, right?

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:39.720
Yeah, they said they'd be back around six.

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:41.240
It must be rough being a senior,

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:43.060
having to hit the books even on New Year's Eve.

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:46.300
They don't have much time until the entrance exams, after all.

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:49.060
They might be feeling anxious or under pressure.

00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:54.400
But they don't <i>seem</i> tense when they're at Hidamari Apartments.

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:57.280
Maybe they're just being considerate.

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:02.760
How about we all act tense?

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:04.300
Well, that'd be kind of...

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:10.000
I hope Sae-san and Hiro-san get into the colleges they want.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:11.040
Yeah!

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:13.800
But if they don't...

00:05:14.920 --> 00:05:19.930
Will they stay here another year until they can try again?

00:05:19.930 --> 00:05:21.930
Nazuna, what a horrible thing to say!

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:23.720
S-Sorry!

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:26.720
Sorry.

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:30.400
I couldn't help but imagine how nice that would be.

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:39.200
You should go mail the ones you've finished.

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:41.860
But it's so cold outside!

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:42.530
Hey, guys!

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:45.290
Let's find a way to warm ourselves up after mailing out the New Year's cards!

00:05:45.290 --> 00:05:46.540
Huh?

00:05:46.890 --> 00:05:49.960
Ba-bam, bam, ba-bam!

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:51.980
This is so warm!

00:05:51.980 --> 00:05:53.660
It feels nice.

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:56.780
Taking a bath on New Year's Eve feels special.

00:05:56.780 --> 00:05:57.820
It sure does.

00:05:57.820 --> 00:06:00.680
I scrubbed down my body thoroughly.

00:06:01.010 --> 00:06:03.860
To ring in a refreshing new year,

00:06:03.860 --> 00:06:07.860
we cleanse ourselves of what has collected on us over the past year,

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:10.690
even though we wash our body every day.

00:06:12.530 --> 00:06:15.480
It sounds deep when you say it, Nazuna-dono.

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:17.900
Or at least, I feel that way.

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:20.650
Well, it's like a sort of purification ceremony.

00:06:23.410 --> 00:06:26.980
How did you spend your New Year's Eve back home?

00:06:26.980 --> 00:06:28.800
I always stayed home with my family.

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:31.290
This is my first year spending the day like this.

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:32.290
Me too.

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:38.000
As for me, none of my family will even be on Earth the moment the new year hits.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:38.550
What?!

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:42.020
Because they jump when the date changes, right?

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:44.050
I did that in elementary school.

00:06:44.050 --> 00:06:46.310
I see!

00:06:46.310 --> 00:06:48.080
But the <i>entire</i> family?

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:49.060
Look at me!

00:06:50.630 --> 00:06:52.310
I'm holding up the Earth!

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:56.600
Whoa!

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:02.940
I hope these make it to their destinations safely.

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:04.070
Nazuna!

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:05.820
Wait for me!

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:12.220
It's snowing!

00:07:12.220 --> 00:07:13.670
Hey, it is!

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:19.170
Oh!

00:07:19.170 --> 00:07:20.920
It's the landlady!

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:22.900
Oh, you're all together out here!

00:07:22.900 --> 00:07:24.260
Hello!

00:07:24.260 --> 00:07:27.430
Perfect timing. I was about to come see you.

00:07:27.430 --> 00:07:29.430
Here are some soba noodles for tonight!

00:07:29.430 --> 00:07:30.600
Yay!

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:31.940
Year-end soba, huh?

00:07:31.940 --> 00:07:33.190
Thank you so much!

00:07:33.190 --> 00:07:35.900
You're ringing in the new year at Hidamari Apartments, right?

00:07:35.900 --> 00:07:36.800
We are!

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:37.400
Oh!

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:38.400
Landlady!

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:41.000
Thank you for putting up with us over the past year.

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:42.120
What are you saying?

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:43.320
Thank <i>you</i> for your patronage.

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:46.160
I hope to have you at my apartments for another year.

00:07:50.290 --> 00:07:53.800
I guess you'll be staying up late tonight, but don't make it a habit!

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:55.040
Got it!

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:57.540
Happy New Year!

00:07:59.800 --> 00:08:02.640
Sae-san and Hiro-san are back!

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:05.130
Remember to act tense!

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:07.050
Whoa, we're really doing that?

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:09.100
We're back!

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:10.340
Hi there.

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:11.240
We're done!

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:12.810
Is everyone here?

00:08:17.710 --> 00:08:18.650
Huh?

00:08:19.130 --> 00:08:21.160
Did you get into a fight or something?

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:24.190
You can tell us if there's something wrong.

00:08:25.320 --> 00:08:27.600
We just made them worry about us more!

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:29.950
I told you it was a bad idea!

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:34.580
Serving year-end soba!

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:35.580
Oh!

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:37.540
Landlady gave us noodles.

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:39.080
Thanks!

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:40.340
It looks delicious!

00:08:41.090 --> 00:08:41.840
Huh?

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:49.090
The chopsticks dropped out.

00:08:50.100 --> 00:08:52.100
Nazuna-chan, be careful what you say!

00:08:54.350 --> 00:08:56.100
Oh, I'm sorry!

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:00.660
Let's eat!

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:04.520
We made a lot, so feel free to ask for more!

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:05.110
Okay!

00:09:05.550 --> 00:09:10.950
They say that you'll have bad luck with money if you don't finish your year-end soba before the new year.

00:09:16.330 --> 00:09:18.060
Thanks for the food!

00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:21.420
Now we just have to wait for the new year.

00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:24.960
Oh yeah, everyone's starting their year off here this time, huh?

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:28.300
Nori, Nazuna, you've already been back home, right?

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:29.100
Yes.

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:32.220
We both came back right after Christmas.

00:09:32.220 --> 00:09:36.700
We heard you don't have senior study sessions for the first three days of the New Year,

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:39.190
so we thought we should spend them together.

00:09:41.110 --> 00:09:44.000
The chili peppers we put in the soba are getting to me now.

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:45.200
This late?

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:49.810
Oh, excuse me.

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:50.700
Hello?

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:52.800
Oh, Yuno?

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:54.280
I was wondering how you're doing.

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:58.500
Dad? We just finished eating year-end soba.

00:09:58.500 --> 00:09:59.250
What's up?

00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:01.180
Well, it's not me,

00:10:01.180 --> 00:10:05.460
but Nyanta was feeling sad that you didn't come home this year.

00:10:05.460 --> 00:10:06.460
Nyanta?

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:08.230
Come on, Nyanta!

00:10:08.230 --> 00:10:09.520
Meow!

00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:11.960
Hear that? He's been howling all day.

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:12.840
Honey!

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:15.470
Why are you calling Yuno?

00:10:18.020 --> 00:10:20.140
Yunocchi, what's wrong?

00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:22.480
It was from Nyanta.

00:10:26.230 --> 00:10:27.730
Clang!

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:30.320
I can hear the New Year's Eve bell!

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:32.740
Yeah, the year's finally coming to an end.

00:10:32.740 --> 00:10:35.160
It's still snowing.

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:36.240
I wonder if the snow will pile up.

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:40.500
What? That'd mean I might slip on ice.

00:10:43.630 --> 00:10:47.130
You don't have to worry about us too much.

00:10:47.130 --> 00:10:49.630
Yeah, that'd just bother us.

00:10:54.890 --> 00:10:57.630
They're sound asleep.

00:10:57.630 --> 00:11:00.220
They must've been tired from all the studying.

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:01.820
Let's not wake them up.

00:11:01.150 --> 00:11:03.110
Ten, nine...

00:11:01.820 --> 00:11:04.500
Oh, the year's about to change!

00:11:03.110 --> 00:11:05.150
Eight, seven...

00:11:05.150 --> 00:11:08.220
Six, five, four...

00:11:08.220 --> 00:11:11.020
Three, two, one...

00:11:11.530 --> 00:11:14.500
Happy New Year!

00:11:23.130 --> 00:11:24.880
There are quite a few people here!

00:11:24.880 --> 00:11:26.220
Wow!

00:11:26.220 --> 00:11:27.620
It's so lively!

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:30.680
It's my first time visiting the shrine for New Year's while it's still dark out.

00:11:30.680 --> 00:11:31.550
Me too!

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:32.250
Wait!

00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:35.230
Yuno-san, you're holding that like you've had it forever!

00:11:35.230 --> 00:11:37.000
When did you buy that?!

00:11:37.680 --> 00:11:39.250
This Dharma doll?

00:11:39.250 --> 00:11:40.750
A few minutes ago!

00:11:41.660 --> 00:11:43.130
Our eyes just met.

00:11:43.130 --> 00:11:45.670
You haven't even filled in an eye yet!

00:11:54.770 --> 00:11:56.570
What about the fortune slips?

00:11:56.570 --> 00:11:58.520
Let's draw them once everybody's here.

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:03.570
Nazuna, this way!

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:06.490
Yeah!

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:12.070
You done?

00:12:12.070 --> 00:12:12.830
Yeah!

00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:14.960
All right, looks good.

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:17.960
Oh, it's Hiro-san!

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:19.590
Hello? Hiro-san?

00:12:19.590 --> 00:12:21.630
Yuno-san? Where are you right now?

00:12:21.630 --> 00:12:23.630
We're at the shrine.

00:12:23.630 --> 00:12:24.710
I see!

00:12:24.710 --> 00:12:26.510
I was getting worried.

00:12:26.510 --> 00:12:28.650
Jeez, you shouldn't have left us behind!

00:12:28.650 --> 00:12:30.830
Oh, s-sorry!

00:12:30.830 --> 00:12:33.170
You were both sound asleep.

00:12:34.100 --> 00:12:35.430
I wasn't being serious.

00:12:35.430 --> 00:12:38.470
Do you mind if we join you?

00:12:38.470 --> 00:12:40.250
Of course not! We'll be waiting.

00:12:41.960 --> 00:12:44.130
Did Sae-san and Hiro-san wake up?

00:12:44.130 --> 00:12:44.870
Yeah!

00:12:44.870 --> 00:12:46.590
They'll be here soon.

00:12:46.590 --> 00:12:49.910
They're giving out zenzai red bean soup over there!

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:51.890
Oh, that's nice.

00:12:51.890 --> 00:12:53.790
Should we get some too?

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:54.490
Yes!

00:12:57.040 --> 00:12:58.890
It's so warm!

00:12:58.890 --> 00:13:00.550
It smells nice.

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:02.150
I'm digging in!

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:05.400
It's so sweet!

00:13:05.400 --> 00:13:06.760
It makes me warm.

00:13:08.140 --> 00:13:09.800
This is splendid!

00:13:09.800 --> 00:13:12.640
That's also "zenzai," isn't it?

00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:13.760
Is it?

00:13:13.760 --> 00:13:16.050
When you write "zenzai" in kanji,

00:13:16.050 --> 00:13:18.020
it can also be read as "yokikana," or "splendid."

00:13:18.020 --> 00:13:20.020
You're so knowledgeable!

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:23.400
Nah, I just saw it on TV yesterday.

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:26.030
This zenzai is delicious!

00:13:26.030 --> 00:13:28.070
This is splendid!

00:13:28.070 --> 00:13:30.030
This is splendid indeed!

00:13:34.280 --> 00:13:35.570
It's beautiful!

00:13:35.570 --> 00:13:38.290
You never get tired of watching fire.

00:13:38.290 --> 00:13:41.330
I just noticed it stopped snowing.

00:13:41.330 --> 00:13:43.420
It didn't really pile up.

00:13:44.580 --> 00:13:45.990
Thanks for waiting.

00:13:47.170 --> 00:13:48.850
Sae-san, Hiro-san!

00:13:48.850 --> 00:13:51.530
Happy New Year!

00:13:51.530 --> 00:13:53.750
Happy New Year.

00:13:53.750 --> 00:13:55.430
Did you rest well?

00:13:55.430 --> 00:13:56.690
Thanks to you.

00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:58.180
Thanks, guys.

00:13:58.430 --> 00:13:59.750
It's so warm!

00:13:59.750 --> 00:14:02.830
We're done with the shrine visit.

00:14:02.830 --> 00:14:04.900
You can get some zenzai over there.

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:07.900
Should we do the shrine visit too?

00:14:07.900 --> 00:14:09.150
Yeah.

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:14.650
Sae, what did you wish for?

00:14:14.650 --> 00:14:17.710
Well, college, among other things.

00:14:18.560 --> 00:14:19.410
What about you?

00:14:20.120 --> 00:14:21.160
It's a secret!

00:14:21.160 --> 00:14:23.670
What? That's no fair!

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:30.290
Where should we hang ours?

00:14:30.290 --> 00:14:32.710
Let's hang them alongside everyone else's.

00:14:32.710 --> 00:14:33.910
Oh yeah.

00:14:34.340 --> 00:14:36.430
Did you get wish plaques?

00:14:36.430 --> 00:14:38.070
Where are yours?

00:14:38.070 --> 00:14:40.630
Where did we hang ours again?

00:14:40.630 --> 00:14:42.950
They already got lost behind the others.

00:14:42.950 --> 00:14:43.830
Yeah.

00:14:46.190 --> 00:14:48.250
Let's open them on the count of two.

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:50.970
I'm so nervous!

00:14:50.970 --> 00:14:54.200
I got "great blessing" last year.

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:56.450
One, two...

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:59.070
Oh, I got future blessing.

00:14:59.070 --> 00:15:04.620
"As you gradually approach a time of good luck, your wishes shall come true," it says.

00:15:04.620 --> 00:15:05.960
I got middle blessing.

00:15:06.320 --> 00:15:10.750
"Study hard without worrying too much," is what mine says.

00:15:10.750 --> 00:15:12.470
That's a relief.

00:15:12.470 --> 00:15:13.090
Yeah!

00:15:14.340 --> 00:15:16.090
I drew future blessing too.

00:15:16.440 --> 00:15:18.690
It says I'll safely deliver my baby.

00:15:18.690 --> 00:15:20.600
I have small blessing.

00:15:22.540 --> 00:15:23.910
Tada!

00:15:23.910 --> 00:15:25.350
Super blessing!

00:15:25.350 --> 00:15:26.100
Super blessing?!

00:15:26.100 --> 00:15:27.590
I've never seen one of these before!

00:15:27.590 --> 00:15:29.990
Miya-chan, you got super blessing again this year?

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:32.190
You always have such good luck.

00:15:32.190 --> 00:15:32.990
How about you, Yuno?

00:15:33.990 --> 00:15:35.360
Yunocchi?

00:15:38.460 --> 00:15:40.990
I-I drew great curse.

00:15:40.990 --> 00:15:43.070
Yuno-san, don't get depressed.

00:15:43.070 --> 00:15:44.370
Yeah, Yuno.

00:15:44.940 --> 00:15:47.830
Great curse means, "No more fortune will escape you."

00:15:47.830 --> 00:15:50.630
Something along the lines of, "It will only get better."

00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:52.250
Really?

00:15:52.250 --> 00:15:54.610
Great curse is pretty rare.

00:15:54.610 --> 00:15:57.270
Yunocchi, you won a rare item!

00:15:57.270 --> 00:15:59.090
Yuno-san, cheer up!

00:16:00.390 --> 00:16:06.450
So, Yuno, let's go tie that up on the sacred tree so the god will help us.

00:16:06.450 --> 00:16:07.150
Okay.

00:16:13.400 --> 00:16:15.650
I wish for things to go well.

00:16:15.650 --> 00:16:17.770
Yunocchi, it'll be all right!

00:16:17.770 --> 00:16:20.780
Weep, weep, weep...

00:16:18.800 --> 00:16:19.780
This voice is...

00:16:21.280 --> 00:16:22.910
Yoshinoya-sensei!

00:16:22.910 --> 00:16:28.170
Oh, hi everyone! Happy New Year!

00:16:28.170 --> 00:16:30.930
Happy New Year.

00:16:30.930 --> 00:16:32.810
What happened, Sensei?

00:16:32.810 --> 00:16:34.170
First tears of the year?

00:16:34.170 --> 00:16:35.420
Yes.

00:16:35.420 --> 00:16:38.890
I drew curse again this year.

00:16:38.890 --> 00:16:39.930
Oh my.

00:16:39.930 --> 00:16:40.930
Sensei!

00:16:40.930 --> 00:16:44.440
It was worse for me. I drew great curse!

00:16:44.440 --> 00:16:46.430
Oh, you got curse too?

00:16:46.430 --> 00:16:49.390
We're so out of luck.

00:16:49.390 --> 00:16:53.690
Good things happen if you tie it with your tongue, right?

00:16:53.690 --> 00:16:54.690
Huh?

00:16:54.690 --> 00:16:56.170
That's not right!

00:17:05.200 --> 00:17:06.200
Sae!

00:17:06.200 --> 00:17:07.490
She's here.

00:17:07.490 --> 00:17:11.570
Huh? That wish plaque looks like it was just hung.

00:17:11.570 --> 00:17:13.460
She might still be around.

00:17:13.460 --> 00:17:14.210
Huh?

00:17:14.210 --> 00:17:17.330
We'll be over there having some zenzai,

00:17:17.330 --> 00:17:18.450
so why don't you go look for her?

00:17:18.450 --> 00:17:20.750
I-It's all right.

00:17:20.750 --> 00:17:22.720
I'm here with you guys.

00:17:23.720 --> 00:17:25.550
Go find her!

00:17:25.550 --> 00:17:28.230
You might get to wish her a happy new year!

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:32.730
I-If you insist, I'll take a walk around the shrine and look.

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:44.740
Huh?

00:17:44.740 --> 00:17:46.120
Hey, Yuno-chan!

00:17:46.120 --> 00:17:47.620
Oh, Landlady!

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:50.070
Happy New Year!

00:17:50.070 --> 00:17:52.870
Oh, Happy New Year.

00:17:52.870 --> 00:17:56.290
Landlady, Happy New Year!

00:17:56.290 --> 00:17:58.130
Oh, if it isn't Sensei!

00:17:58.130 --> 00:18:00.950
Thanks for taking care of these kids all the time.

00:18:00.950 --> 00:18:03.890
Please keep teaching and guiding them well this year!

00:18:03.890 --> 00:18:04.640
Of course!

00:18:06.140 --> 00:18:08.140
You're drunk, aren't you?

00:18:08.140 --> 00:18:09.270
Well...

00:18:09.270 --> 00:18:11.610
I was invited to a year-end mahjong game.

00:18:11.610 --> 00:18:14.980
I got all the good chips. This will be a great year!

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:16.610
Chips?

00:18:21.610 --> 00:18:25.160
You can look at the year's first sunrise from here.

00:18:25.160 --> 00:18:26.930
Since we're here anyway, why don't we stay and watch?

00:18:26.930 --> 00:18:27.870
Yeah.

00:18:29.370 --> 00:18:30.620
Sae!

00:18:30.620 --> 00:18:33.120
Oh, Natsume!

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:37.880
F-Fancy seeing you here.

00:18:38.440 --> 00:18:39.630
Yeah.

00:18:39.630 --> 00:18:42.410
H-Happy New Year.

00:18:43.340 --> 00:18:45.170
Happy New Year!

00:18:45.170 --> 00:18:46.640
Let's have another great year.

00:18:49.390 --> 00:18:51.940
Y-Yeah, let's.

00:18:51.940 --> 00:18:55.900
Do you want to watch the first sunrise of the year with us?

00:18:56.280 --> 00:18:57.090
Yeah!

00:18:58.180 --> 00:18:59.320
Natsume-san!

00:18:59.760 --> 00:19:02.310
Happy New Year!

00:19:02.310 --> 00:19:04.240
Happy New Year.

00:19:10.410 --> 00:19:11.750
It has begun.

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:13.540
Principal?!

00:19:15.540 --> 00:19:19.050
It's a sacred daybreak that happens only once a year.

00:19:46.070 --> 00:19:49.310
There's a proverb that goes, "New Year's Day is the key to the year."

00:19:49.310 --> 00:19:52.890
It means the beginning is important for anything.

00:19:52.890 --> 00:19:54.330
Got it!

00:19:54.330 --> 00:19:56.270
Third-years!

00:19:56.270 --> 00:19:59.530
You won't get to be high school girls for much longer!

00:19:59.530 --> 00:20:01.710
Make sure you don't leave any regrets behind!

00:20:01.710 --> 00:20:02.800
Okay.

00:20:03.800 --> 00:20:06.550
I'll get back to my other friends.

00:20:06.550 --> 00:20:08.570
See you, Natsume-san.

00:20:08.570 --> 00:20:11.680
Natsume, let's both do our best to get into college.

00:20:11.680 --> 00:20:12.680
Yeah!

00:20:14.430 --> 00:20:17.350
I-I didn't need to be told that!

00:20:17.440 --> 00:20:18.710
See you!

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:22.650
All right.

00:20:22.650 --> 00:20:25.470
I should go attend New Year's parties.

00:20:25.470 --> 00:20:26.690
Right now?

00:20:26.690 --> 00:20:28.070
You're so tireless.

00:20:28.070 --> 00:20:29.820
Sure I am!

00:20:29.820 --> 00:20:33.090
And Yunocchi... Are you getting sleepy now?

00:20:33.090 --> 00:20:34.770
Yeah, a bit.

00:20:34.770 --> 00:20:36.530
You've been up all night, right?

00:20:36.530 --> 00:20:39.330
Then let's go back and get some sleep.

00:20:41.880 --> 00:20:43.710
Nazuna, your mouth's so big.

00:20:44.460 --> 00:20:46.470
Nori-chan!

00:20:51.160 --> 00:20:55.030
Then let's eat zouni mochi soup after some sleep.

00:20:55.030 --> 00:20:57.810
Oh yeah, I want three mochis!

00:20:57.810 --> 00:20:58.770
Got it.

00:20:58.770 --> 00:21:00.250
Okay, see you all in a bit.

00:21:00.250 --> 00:21:02.230
Sleep tight!

00:21:05.740 --> 00:21:07.490
It's my first bath of the year!

00:21:07.490 --> 00:21:09.490
Happy New Year!

00:21:10.990 --> 00:21:15.250
I'll finally become a third-year this year.

00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:19.190
That means I'll be applying to colleges.

00:21:19.920 --> 00:21:24.250
I should figure out what I want to do like Sae-san and Hiro-san.

00:21:26.580 --> 00:21:29.010
Sometimes I get worried or feel depressed,

00:21:29.920 --> 00:21:31.950
but there are people who help me get over it,

00:21:31.950 --> 00:21:35.390
people who are there for me at Hidamari Apartments.

00:21:50.000 --> 00:21:51.660
So I'm sure I'll be all right.

00:22:00.820 --> 00:22:04.670
I hope this will be a great year for everybody!

00:22:07.010 --> 00:22:10.010
December 31st - January 1st

00:22:07.010 --> 00:22:10.010
The End

